Introduction to Sentiment Analysis
You might be wondering: “what is sentiment analysis?” In reputation and review management, sentiment analysis is the process of computationally identifying and categorizing customer feedback to determine a customer’s experience towards a particular aspect of your business, product, or service. At a high level, sentiment analysis gauges whether the experience the customer is writing about is positive or negative.

Analyzing unstructured data (like customer reviews) has traditionally been a very time-intensive process. But how can you use that data as a business owner or manager to improve your products and services? Are there more efficient ways to analyze customer feedback rather than sifting through those manually?

